<title>USA: U.S. JULY RETAIL SALES ROSE 0.6 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>U.S. JULY RETAIL SALES ROSE 0.6 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  July   June--(Prev)  July97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.6    0.7    0.5	4.5</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.5    0.4    0.3	4.3</p>
<p> Auto Sales		1.0    1.4    1.1	5.0</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.7    1.1    0.5	4.8</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.6    0.4    0.4	4.2</p>
<p> Furniture Stores     -0.4    0.2    1.5	4.8</p>
<p> Building Materials    0.9    0.9   -1.2	6.7</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: July    June-(Previous)    May--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 212.08   210.74  210.30   209.37  209.31</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    160.95   160.10  159.89   159.45  159.46</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    51.13    50.64   50.41    49.93   49.85</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 86.30    85.68   85.13    84.76   84.70</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   125.78   125.06  125.17   124.61  124.61</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.67    11.72   11.87    11.69   11.69</p>
<p> Building Materials  12.24    12.13   11.91    12.02   12.05</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  July   June--(Prev)  July97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores  0.7    0.8    0.8	6.8</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.8    0.8    0.9	8.2</p>
<p> Food Stores	     0.4   -0.2   -0.1	1.3</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	  0.4   -0.2   -0.2	0.9</p>
<p> Gas Stations	    0.8   -0.1   -0.9	1.5</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	  0.2    1.2   Unch	3.1</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places	0.4    0.4    1.1	4.1</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.9    0.3    0.3	8.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: July    June-(Previous)     May----(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.76    27.56    27.54     27.35   27.33</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.89    21.72    21.69     21.55   21.50</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.83    35.71    35.85     35.76   35.87</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.76    33.61    33.73     33.69   33.79</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  12.93    12.83    12.68     12.84   12.79</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.75     9.73     9.60	9.62    9.61</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.38    20.31    20.47     20.23   20.24</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.19     8.12     8.11	8.10    8.08</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected July retail sales to rise 0.7 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised May auto sales to a 1.0 percent decrease from a 1.2 percent drop.</p>
</text>
